09:02.450 --> 09:08.110
So that means we will not go and store the data like this, ascending from the lowest sales to the highest

09:08.110 --> 09:10.230
sales, we're going to go and switch it.

09:10.230 --> 09:14.510
So we're going to go and sort the data from the highest sales to the lowest sales.

09:14.830 --> 09:18.150
And with that, the first value is going to be the highest sales.

09:18.350 --> 09:22.390
So let me just rename it highest sales.

09:22.430 --> 09:23.630
Let's give it like two.

09:23.990 --> 09:26.070
So let's go and execute this.

09:26.070 --> 09:31.590
And now you can see over here we got the exact same results because we sorted the data differently and

09:31.590 --> 09:32.990
we get the first value.

09:32.990 --> 09:36.510
So this is going to give you the exact same effect like the last value.

09:36.790 --> 09:40.750
And as you can see I don't have to define now any window or something like that.

09:40.910 --> 09:45.190
I can stick with the default frame but just twisting the order by.

09:45.470 --> 09:49.430
So this is how you can do it as well using only the first value.

09:49.430 --> 09:54.030
So now just for the sake of this task, there's as well another possibility in how to solve this.

09:54.030 --> 09:56.710
